The issue is BaseSettings.setdefault inherited from MutableMapping but broken due to __getitem__ returning None instead of raising KeyError when missing. To fix, implement setdefault method in BaseSettings that uses self.set appropriately. So need to modify scrapy/settings/__init__.py, adding setdefault method to BaseSettings. Possibly also adjust __getitem__? But better to define setdefault to bypass __getitem__.

Add method:

def setdefault(self, opt_name, default=None):
    if opt_name not in self:
        self.set(opt_name, default)
        return default
    else:
        return self[opt_name]

Signature maybe with priority param? Not needed. Tests may use .setdefault on Settings objects. Let's search tests for setdefault on settings.Search tests for ".setdefault(" with BaseSettings.
